/// <summary>
/// The CSSLayerStatementRule represents a @layer statement rule. Unlike CSSLayerBlockRule, it doesn&apos;t contain other rules and merely defines one or several layers by providing their names. This rule allows you to explicitly declare the ordering layer that is in an apparent way at the beginning of a CSS file: the layer order is defined by the order of first occurrence of each layer name. Declaring them with a statement allows the reader to understand the layer order. It also allows inline and imported layers to be interleaved, which is not possible when using the CSSLayerBlockRule syntax.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// <see href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSLayerStatementRule">MDN Web Docs: CSSLayerStatementRule</see>
/// </remarks>
