    /// <summary>
    /// The TimeEvent.initTimeEvent() method initializes the value of a TimeEvent created using Document.createEvent(). This method may only be called before the event has been dispatched via EventTarget.dispatchEvent(). If called multiple times, the final call takes precedence. Note: Document.createEvent() is deprecated in favor of event constructors, but TimeEvent has no dedicated constructor. CustomEvent is not a valid replacement, as it does not produce a TimeEvent instance with the interface&apos;s view and detail attributes.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <see href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/TimeEvent/initTimeEvent">MDN Web Docs: TimeEvent.initTimeEvent</see>
